# ============================================================================
#  PHI and patient-derived data — must never enter this repository
# ============================================================================
# Everything below either is patient data or is derived from it row by row.

# Report archives and image crops
cirrus_out/
cirrus_out*/
dw_images/
phase_b_images/
_crop_*/
_check_samples/

# Modelling tables and every extraction product. These carry patient
# identifiers and examination dates in their key columns.
*.csv
*.xlsx
*.xls

# Per-eye predictions, checkpoints, and anything a model wrote
*.npz
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.h5
*.pkl
*.joblib
runs/
build/
step4_work/
experiments/laterality_qfix/step4_work/

# Notebooks: outputs are saved with the source, so a single execution can
# embed a patient identifier or an image that no diff will show.
*.ipynb
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Rendered figures and documents. Figures 1 and 6 contain thickness maps and a
# measured field from a study eye.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.tif
*.tiff
*.pdf
*.docx
*.pptx

# Local secrets and environment
.env
*.key
*.pem
pseudonym_map*
*phi_blocklist*

# ============================================================================
#  Working material that is not part of the reproduction chain
# ============================================================================
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
.DS_Store
*.log
*.out
*.swp

# The manuscript itself is out of scope for this repository (see README).
docs/journal_manuscript/
paper/manuscript/
paper/drafts/

# Internal working notes: audit trails, meeting memos, status reports. They are
# how the work was managed, not how it is reproduced, and several name people.
docs/*
!docs/coordinate_frame_convention.md
# 원고 동반 명세의 §1~§4 발췌. 게이트가 프로토콜 상수와 코호트 표
# 앵커를 여기서 읽으므로, 없으면 복제본에서 check_numbers.py 가
# 근거 없이 MISS 를 낸다. §5~§6 은 비공개 감사 기록이라 빠져 있다.
!docs/CANONICAL_SPEC.md

# ============================================================================
#  Public-repository curation
#
#  The rules above exclude by default. What follows re-admits, one path at a
#  time, the artefacts a reader needs in order to check a printed number. Each
#  exception is a deliberate decision, not a pattern: a frozen result is
#  aggregate over 240 or 37 eyes and holds no per-eye row.
# ============================================================================

# The frozen values the manuscript quotes. Aggregate only; see
# paper/results_frozen/README.md for what was removed on the way in.
!paper/results_frozen/
!paper/results_frozen/*.json
!paper/results_frozen/README.md

# Report region coordinates for the extraction step. Page geometry, no data.
!cirrus_regions.json

# Configuration. Constants only.
!config/params.yaml

# The number gate's configuration. scripts/check_numbers.py reads exactly these
# two files under verify/ and nothing else; the rest of that directory is the
# internal defect audit, its run logs, and a test fixture that names a real
# institution (verify/test_gate.py:45), so it stays out.
verify/*
!verify/exceptions.yaml
!verify/placeholder_patterns.yaml
